@namespace SpaceSails.Client.Pages.Stations
@using SpaceSails.Core
@*
    #251 · THE AIM ROSETTE, ON ITS OWN FILE.

    Moved out of Pages/Stations/TrackingPost.razor by PURE MOTION — the block between the two fences
    below is the block that stood in the desk, character for character, at the indentation it had
    there. Every member it reads is a [Parameter] carrying the desk's own member UNDER THAT MEMBER'S
    OWN NAME (a field keeps its underscore, a method arrives as a delegate, a callback as itself), so
    the markup moved without a rewrite and TrackingPostMarkup splices the desk back byte for byte.

    The .razor.css beside this file carries no rules; it is there to give the component
    TrackingPost.razor.css's OWN scope (b-9ekzcovohe, pinned in SpaceSails.Client.csproj). That sheet
    has forty rules and not one `::deep` among them, so every one of them is scope-dependent: without
    the carrier, every rule that styles this surface would stop matching the moment the markup moved
    out of the desk — no build error, no test, the block just renders unstyled.

    The dial is drawn from TelescopeModel.Range itself rather than a re-derived formula, so the picture
    can never drift from what the sweep logic actually does (TrackingPost.Rosette.cs says why at length).
    All seven members below are that file's, arriving under their own names.
*@
@* ── MARKUP BEGINS · verbatim from TrackingPost.razor ─────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
            <div class="tracking-rosette flex-shrink-0 @(FullScreen ? "tracking-rosette-big" : "")">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 200 200" class="tracking-rosette-svg" aria-label="Sun-relative detection range">
                    <polygon points="@RosettePolygonPoints()" class="tracking-rosette-envelope" />
                    <polygon points="@WedgePolygonPoints()" class="tracking-rosette-wedge @(_activeJob is not null ? "tracking-rosette-wedge-active" : "")" />
                    @* M27: bearing vectors from the ship to every tracked target — threats dashed red. *@
                    @foreach ((double x, double y, string color, bool threat) in TrackedTargetDots())
                    {
                        <line x1="100" y1="100" x2="@x" y2="@y"
                              class="@(threat ? "tracking-vector tracking-vector-threat" : "tracking-vector")"
                              stroke="@color" />
                    }
                    @foreach ((double x, double y, string color, bool threat) in TrackedTargetDots())
                    {
                        <circle cx="@x" cy="@y" r="@(threat ? 4 : 3)" fill="@color" />
                    }
                    @* M27: the prograde arrow — which way the ship is actually flying. *@
                    @if (ProgradePoint() is { } fwd)
                    {
                        <line x1="100" y1="100" x2="@fwd.X" y2="@fwd.Y" class="tracking-prograde-line" />
                        <circle cx="@fwd.X" cy="@fwd.Y" r="2.5" class="tracking-prograde-tip" />
                    }
                    <line x1="100" y1="100" x2="100" y2="14" class="tracking-rosette-sunline" />
                    <text x="100" y="10" class="tracking-rosette-label" text-anchor="middle">☉</text>
                    <circle cx="100" cy="100" r="4" class="tracking-rosette-ship" />
                </svg>
                <div class="text-secondary tracking-heading-line">@HeadingLine()</div>
            </div>
@* ── MARKUP ENDS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
